<BlogPost title="New from Shiloh — 1¼″ Edge-Banded Shelf" description="Shiloh's new 1¼-inch edge-banded plywood shelf offers a clean solution for open cabinetry with veneered wood on all four sides." author="Ben Miller" publishedDate="2026-02-05" heroImage="/images/blog/shiloh-edge-banded-shelf-1.webp" modifiedDate="2026-10-29">

<p>Now in production: Shiloh's new 1¼" Edge-Banded Shelf offers a clean, high-quality plywood shelf solution for open cabinetry and display applications.</p>

<div class="post-images">
  <img src="/images/blog/shiloh-edge-banded-shelf-1.webp" alt="Shiloh Edge-Banded Shelf specification"  width="478" height="268" fetchpriority="high" />
  <img src="/images/blog/shiloh-edge-banded-shelf-2.webp" alt="Shiloh Edge-Banded Shelf detail"  width="1200" height="674" loading="lazy" />
</div>

<h2>Why Designers Will Like It</h2>
<ul>
<li>Solid plywood core with taped veneer edge-banded on all four sides; underside matches the finish</li>
<li>Square corners only (no angles), ideal for Taiga and other contemporary frames</li>
<li>Field-install only — shelves ship loose and are installed on site</li>
</ul>

<h2>Quick Specs</h2>
<ul>
<li>Available only in Shiloh (must be ordered on a Shiloh SKU)</li>
<li>Finishes: Only offered in Stains and Paints on Wood (no laminates)</li>
<li>Max size: 30" D × 48" W — do NOT exceed 48" length</li>
<li>Between cabinets: reduce depth 7/8" to fit behind the frame; order +1/8" width for side recess</li>
<li>Optional PFSL groove (Prep Floating Shelf for Lighting): $100 list — runs full shelf length</li>
<li>Price: $0.314 / in²</li>
<li>Shipping: Not available via express parcel — ships on W.W. Wood Products truck</li>
<li>Oversized shelves may incur a <strong>$550 crate charge</strong> (one shelf per crate)</li>
<li>Custom sizes beyond the 48″ × 30″ standard maximum can be quoted</li>
<li>Grain direction runs with the width (the second dimension)</li>
<li>Not recommended for wet locations</li>
</ul>

<h2>Where It Fits</h2>
<ul>
<li>Frameless and modern open-shelving designs — the finished underside makes it work fully exposed</li>
<li>Bookcases and built-ins that need a thicker, stronger, more substantial shelf</li>
<li>Lit display shelving — pair the PFSL groove with locally sourced LED (see our <a href="/playbook/led-prep-shiloh-eclipse/">LED prep guide</a>)</li>
</ul>

